<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Trowulan</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Trowulan is an archaeological site in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-java">East Java</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indonesia">Indonesia</a>, identified as the location of the capital of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/majapahit-empire">Majapahit Empire</a>. Its extensive remains include temples, gateways, canals and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/reservoir">reservoirs</a>. The capital was established there during early consolidation and lost prominence by the early sixteenth century as administrative centres relocated.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/trowulan.jpg" alt="Trowulan" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ivuvisual · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Eksotika_Candi_Bajang_Ratu.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
